[Term]
id: ARO:0000016
name: aminoglycoside antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Aminoglycosides are a group of antibiotics that are mostly effective against Gram-negative bacteria. These molecules consist of aminated sugars attached to a dibasic cyclitol. Aminoglycosides work by binding to the bacterial 30S ribosomal subunit (some work by binding to the 50S subunit), inhibiting the translocation of the peptidyl-tRNA from the A-site to the P-site and also causing misreading of mRNA, leaving the bacterium unable to synthesize proteins vital to its growth." [PMID:11083623, PMID:8385262, PMID:10103173]
is_a: ARO:1000003 ! antibiotic molecule
property_value: classified_as_drug_class

[Term]
id: ARO:0000017
name: lincosamide antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Lincosamides (e.g. lincomycin, clindamycin) are a class of drugs which bind to the 23s portion of the 50S subunit of bacterial ribosomes. This interaction inhibits early elongation of peptide chains by inhibiting the transpeptidase reaction, acting similarly to macrolides." [PMID:10582867, PMID:15135500]
is_a: ARO:1000003 ! antibiotic molecule
synonym: "lincosamide" EXACT []
property_value: classified_as_drug_class

