property_value: classified_as_antibiotic

[Term]
id: ARO:0000026
name: streptogramin antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Streptogramin antibiotics are natural products produced by various members of the Streptomyces genus. These antibiotics bind to the P site of the 50S subunit of bacterial ribosomes to inhibit protein synthesis. The family consists of two subgroups, type A and type B, which are simultaneously produced by the same bacterial species in a ratio of roughly 70:30." [PMID:15700955]
is_a: ARO:1000003 ! antibiotic molecule
property_value: classified_as_drug_class

[Term]
id: ARO:0000027
name: roxithromycin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Roxithromycin is a semi-synthetic, 14-carbon ring macrolide antibiotic derived from erythromycin. It is used to treat respiratory tract, urinary and soft tissue infections. Roxithromycin may possess bacteriocidal activity, particularly at higher concentrations by binding to the 50S subunit of the bacterial 70S rRNA complex, protein synthesis and subsequently structure/function processes critical for life or replication are inhibited." [PMID:15980346, PMID:10582867]
