[Term]
id: ARO:3000134
name: edeine B
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Edeine B is a subtype of the peptide antibiotic edeine, composed of beta-tyr, beta-ser, diaminopropionic acid, diaminohydroxyazelaic acid, glycine, and guanylspermidine. Edeine B is a mixture of edeine B1 and its inactive isomer, edeine B2.  Edeines bind to the 30S subunit to block fMet-tRNA interaction at the P site, inhibiting protein synthesis and subsequent structure/function processes critical for life or replication. Edeine B has also been shown to inhibit septation and cause filamentous morphology, also leading to cell death." [PMID:4984939, PMID:20410587, PMID:70202]
is_a: ARO:3000119 ! edeine
is_a: ARO:3009657 ! nonribosomal peptide antibiotics
xref: PubChem:446232
