[Term]
id: ARO:3000707
name: antibiotic mixture
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Mixtures of antibiotics are commonly used clinically. These mixtures link to antibiotic molecules that are also listed in their respective families under antibiotic molecules. i.e. 'Gramicidin A' is part of the mixture 'gramicidin D', while 'Gramicidin A' is also a 'gramicidin', which is a 'peptide antibiotic'." []
is_a: ARO:1000003 ! antibiotic molecule

[Term]
id: ARO:3000708
name: antibiotic target
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Antibiotic targets are components of the bacterial or fungal cell. Bacterial targets are usually significantly different from their eukaryotic counterparts to allow for selective antibacterial activity. Exceptions include antibiotics that are converted to an active form inside the bacterium. Resistance mechanisms may modify these targets to protect bacteria or fungi from the effects of antibiotics." []
is_a: ARO:1000001 ! process or component of antibiotic biology or chemistry

[Term]
id: ARO:3000709
name: cell wall synthesis enzyme targeted by antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cell wall biosynthesis provides bacteria with a layer of peptidoglycan that provides rigidity and protects the cell from lysis due to osmotic pressure. Cell wall structures vary significantly between Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria, while mycobacteria have a unique cell wall composition." [PMID:1436736]
is_a: ARO:3000708 ! antibiotic target

[Term]
id: ARO:3000711
name: protein synthesis machinery targeted by antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Protein synthesis in bacteria is accomplished by cytosolic ribosomes that are structurally different from eukaryotic ribosomes, and thus a target for many antibiotics. By inhibiting ribosomal activity, either by directly binding to the ribosome or interacting with co-factors, antibiotics prevent protein synthesis." []
is_a: ARO:3000708 ! antibiotic target

[Term]
id: ARO:3000712
name: nucleic acid synthesis machinery targeted by antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Bacterial DNA and RNA synthesis includes many enzymes unique to bacteria that are targeted by antibiotics." [PMID:22458504]
is_a: ARO:3000708 ! antibiotic target

[Term]
id: ARO:3000713
name: nucleic acid targeted by antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Nucleic acids can also be targeted by antibiotics. These drugs are usually converted to an active form by enzymes unique to bacteria to prevent toxicity to the host." [PMID:15685195]
is_a: ARO:3000708 ! antibiotic target

[Term]
id: ARO:3000714
name: folate synthesis enzyme targeted by antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Enzymes in the folate synthesis pathway are targeted by two main classes of antibiotics: sulfonamides and diaminopyrimidines. Inhibition of these enzymes block the production of key precursors for nucleotides and amino acids." [PMID:4387360]
is_a: ARO:3000708 ! antibiotic target

[Term]
id: ARO:3000716
name: mycolic acid synthesis enzyme targeted by antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Mycolic acids are produced by mycobacteria. These fatty acids are required for the construction of cell walls. Enzymes that are targeted by antibiotics include synthases, elongases, and dehydrogenases." [PMID:8143118, PMID:1656850]
is_a: ARO:3000708 ! antibiotic target
relationship: targeted_by_antibiotic ARO:3000520 ! isoniazid

[Term]
id: ARO:3000725
name: antibiotic sensitive aftA
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Arabinofuranosyltransferases allow for the polymerization of arabinose to form arabinan. Arabanan is required for formation of mycobacterial cell walls." [PMID:18174142, PMID:19596878]
is_a: ARO:3000709 ! cell wall synthesis enzyme targeted by antibiotic
relationship: targeted_by_antibiotic ARO:3000497 ! ethambutol

[Term]
