[Term]
id: ARO:3000744
name: antibiotic sensitive dihydropteroate synthase
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Dihydropteroate synthase catalyzes the conversion of p-aminobenzoic acid to dihydropteroic acid as part of the tetrahydrofolic acid biosynthetic pathway. Tetrahydrofolic acid is essential for folate synthesis, and a precursor of many nucleotides and amino acids. Inhibiting dihydropteroate leads to slow cell death, as bacteria can survive on existing folate storages for a few generations." [PMID:12111724]
