def: "Azoles are a group of antibiotics, particularly antifungals, that target the cytochrome P450 enzyme sterol 14alpha-demethylase, which converts lanosterol to ergosterol. They are typically fungistatic in yeasts and fungicidal in molds. The two main groups of azoles are imidazoles and triazoles." [PMID:32906036]
